Ensure map stride is at least one full row of pixels

Backport of upstream commit 6a8de891fb00968e5ea79bfa84368ed90b3cfc1d
("Ensure map stride is at least one full row of pixels", #9719) to Pillow
10.3.0. The upstream fix relies on the newer findModeID/ModeID mode
dispatch that does not exist in 10.3.0, so the stride flooring is
reimplemented here on top of the 10.3.0 strcmp/strncmp mode dispatch.

PyImaging_MapBuffer only computed a default stride when the caller passed
stride <= 0. A crafted McIdas area descriptor can supply a small positive
stride that is far smaller than one full row of pixels (xsize * pixelsize).
Row pointers are then laid out at that undersized stride while the buffer
size check uses ysize * stride, so im->image[y] pointers can reference
memory past the end of the mapped buffer (out-of-bounds read). Floor the
stride to at least xsize * pixelsize for every code path so the buffer-size
check reflects the real memory footprint and the image is rejected with
"buffer is not large enough".

